{title: Day Is Done}
{subtitle: Nick Drake}
{comment: Key: Am}
{instrument: ukulele}

{define: Am frets 2 0 0 0}
{define: E7 frets 1 2 0 2}
{define: C frets 0 0 0 3}
{define: G frets 0 2 3 2}
{define: F frets 2 0 1 0}

{c: Intro}
[Am] [E7] [C] [G] [F] [Am] [F] [E7]

{c: Verse 1}
When the [Am]day is done [E7]
Down to earth then [C]sinks the sun [G]
Along with [F]everything that was lost and [Am]won
When the [F]day is done [E7]

{c: Verse 2}
When the [Am]day is done [E7]
Hope so much your [C]race'll be all run [G]
Then you [F]find you've jumped the [Am]gun
Have to [F]go back where you be[Am]gun
When the [F]day is done [Am]

{c: Verse 3}
When the [Am]night is cold [E7]
Some get by and [C]some get old [G]
Just to [F]show life's no made of [Am]gold
When the [Am]night is cold [E7]

{c: Instrumental}
[Am] [E7] [C] [G] [F] [Am] [F] [E7]

{c: Verse 4}
When the [Am]bird has flown [E7]
Got no one to [C]call your own [G]
Got no [F]place to call your [Am]home
When the [F]bird has flown [Am]

{c: Instrumental}
[Am] [E7] [C] [G] [F] [Am] [F] [E7]

{c: Verse 5}
When the [Am]game's been fought [E7]
Newspaper [C]blown cross the court [G]
Lost much [F]sooner than you would've [Am]thought
Now the [F]game's been fought [E7]

{c: Verse 6}
When the [Am]part is through [E7]
Seems so very [C]sad for you [G]
Didn't [F]do the things you were meant to [Am]do
Now there's [F]no time start a[Am]new
Now the [E7]part is through [Am]

{c: Verse 7}
When the [Am]day is done [E7]
Down to earth then [C]sinks the sun [G]
Along with [F]everything that was lost and [Am]won

{c: Outro}
When the [F]day is done [Am]
